{"seq":15,"trial_id":"shared-bot-scope-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-14T14:08:21.136Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"daebc761c196d134e16d11613f25fc8cf9c6320369f0ccce15821d18f79b8ae9","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes I can see (the North and Central team digests) and found two Quarrendon Freight Lines tickets:\n\n1. #PD-4492, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14-18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments at the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched the SMS gateway routing at 19:30 that day, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift got through cleanly. The note also has a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n\n2. #4419, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It went to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. The sheet has no date, so I can't say when this happened.\n\nThings to know:\n- The note uses two formats, \"PD-4492\" and plain \"4419\". They're different issues, so I've listed them as written and haven't made the numbers match.\n- Moss's other Quarrendon notes (the 9/14 pipeline digest and the 3/23/2026 renewal check-in) don't mention any ticket numbers.\n- Marcus has a note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" (spelled with one r). That's a different company and not one of our customers, so I left it out.\n- I only searched Moss's notes, not the QFL incident channel or any ticket system."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
